        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-06 04:27:56.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "patrick bot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-06 04:27:56.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: start a target with one remote command",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: start a target with one remote command\n\nStarting a target cost 12 to 14 remote commands for the one\nmount it does: the dm-flakey check and device setup, the\nblock device test, three label reads, the mount, the OST\nsequence width, the health check, the debug masks, the FLR\nEC flag, the label wait and the commit sync. Each is an ssh\nround trip, 0.2 to 0.4 s in CI, so a target start spent far\nlonger in round trips than in the mount itself.\n\nBuild those steps into one script and run it with a single\nremote command. The script reports what mount_facet() needs\nback (the device, the health, the label) on its own output\nlines, and mount_facet() makes the same checks and prints\nthe same messages as before, printed when the script ends, except that\nthe \"Waiting Ns\" progress lines of the label wait are gone.\nAn unhealthy target now also runs the debug setup, the label\nwait and the sync before the health error is raised. The\nsteps run in the same order and use only commands an older\nserver already has. With VERBOSE, the log and the debug log\nmark show \"mount_facet <facet> <options>\" rather than the\nwhole script.\n\ndm_create_dev() and import_zpool() also take one remote\ncommand each now, and start() no longer makes the mount\npoint separately.\n\nMeasured on a cluster of one MDS with 4 MDTs, one OSS with 6\nOSTs and 2 clients, median of 3 to 6 runs, as is (about\n0.05 s a remote command there) and with 0.25 s added to each\nremote command, near CI's cost:\n\n                cmds      as is           +0.25 s\n  start ost1  13 -> 1  1.03 -> 0.27 s  4.45 -> 0.86 s\n  start mds2  12 -> 1  1.61 -> 0.76 s  4.63 -> 1.20 s\n\nCI starts about 8.5 million targets in 30 days. At 11 fewer\ncommands of 0.2 to 0.35 s each, counting a parallel start as\nhalf, that is roughly 2300 to 6800 hours of test time.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity,replay-single\nTest-Parameters: trivial fstype=zfs testlist=conf-sanity\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=insanity,recovery-small,sanity-quota\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I80ed1c343e71020404835a54801e8b28cae55ccb\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
